{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/203381-integrating-changeling-the-lost-with-cwod","id":203381,"title":"Integrating Changeling: The Lost with cWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-20T19:17:54-07:00","id":203381,"title":"Integrating Changeling: The Lost with cWoD","content":"So, I have a game of cWoD coming up and the GM is interested in bringing in some nWoD stuff, specifically the Lost. Now, I'm passingly familiar with the oWoD metaplot, so I'm wondering how this addition would modify it, aside from making Changelings a more interesting thing to do for NPC's as I find the Lost more interesting than the Dreaming's rendition of them, and Lost's concept better than Dreaming's concept. <br /> <br /> I know the Technocracy would have slightly less reason to go to the Moon but I don't know what else it'd really change outside of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:54:11-07:00","id":203547,"title":"","content":"Nothing. Changeling: the Dreaming always existed on the fringe of the oWoD metaplot, and can be excised with little to no impact. Introducing a set of people who were abducted by alien things from another realm and come back changed by the experience is not, in and of itself, going to affect the overall metaplot, unless you want it to \u2014 in which case it has exactly as much impact as you want it to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T23:44:21-07:00","id":203576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/203381-integrating-changeling-the-lost-with-cwod?p=203547#post203547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing. Changeling: the Dreaming always existed on the fringe of the oWoD metaplot, and can be excised with little to no impact. Introducing a set of people who were abducted by alien things from another realm and come back changed by the experience is not, in and of itself, going to affect the overall metaplot, unless you want it to \u2014 in which case it has exactly as much impact as you want it to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Niiiiiice. So basically Dreaming fluff is pretty irrelevant to the oWoD and can be safely ignored?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:57:14-07:00","id":203603,"title":"","content":"Yep. More generally, the cases where the events of one gameline impact the metaplot of another gameline are rare: you\u2019ve got a few ties between <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Mage</b>, mostly regarding the Tremere; and you\u2019ve got the Year of the Reckoning\u2019s termination of <b>Wraith</b> kicking oWoD\u2019s end-of-the-world metaplot into high gear. But beyond that, interconnectedness among the various gamelines is virtually nil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:59:46-07:00","id":203608,"title":"","content":"Pretty much everything can be safely ignored. Despite the ubiquity of the metaplot, most of the important stuff happens far above the pay grade of standard PCs. It can make fun background, but it doesn't matter to an individual chronicle unless the ST wants it to. I think you're good, at least as far as setting goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T03:38:38-07:00","id":204843,"title":"","content":"Myself I prefer Lost to Dreaming as well. I find an allegory for abuse more fitting the tone of World of Darkness than Peter Paning of Dreaming, to be honest. The whole magic goes away aspect is already covered by Mage anyway. And original fairies of folk legends were usually dicks kidnapping people, like in Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T04:33:09-07:00","id":204866,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t really see <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> as a \u201cmagic goes away\u201d game; the closest it ever got to that was the Revised Edition, and even then it wasn\u2019t really about that. Since we\u2019re stating personal preferences, I like both <b>Changeling</b>s, and I look forward to the day that we get a <b>Changeling Translation Guide</b> that lets me integrate both into the same setting. It can be done, you know: from <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>\u2019s perspective, the protagonists of <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> bear an uncanny resemblance to the mortals that were taken to Arcadia to allow the Sidhe to return to Earth; from <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>\u2019s perspective, the protagonists of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> look very similar to Charlatans. In a more general sense, the protagonists of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> are, in effect, exiles from Arcadia who are trying to go back; while the protagonists of <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> are fugitives from Arcadia who are trying to stay away. <br /> <br /> Bottom line, it doesn\u2019t have to be either/or; the two games are different enough from each other that they can coexist side by side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T17:10:02-07:00","id":217064,"title":"","content":"I actually think you can do different take than the two lines if you treat Changelings as classic Changelings and make them doppelgangers replacing human children spirited away for some reason by some inscrutable beings. Imagine you are such doppelganger, think you are human and everything until the realization you are not human after all suddenly kicks in or that you should have not existed at all. An existential horror combined with questioning whom you really are after all. Those beings who put you in this world offer no answers after all. Oh, and add bizarre powers of course since no WoD splat is complete without them. Obviously not metaphor for puberty and identity confusion.<br /> <br /> (Note I did not namedrop fairies since there should be enigma to those beings if such line / fansplat ever came to being, and after all fair folk in many folk tales ARE inscrutable beings which are enigmatic for mortals and even outright creepy and dangerous depending on circumstances)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T18:08:56-07:00","id":217088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/203381-integrating-changeling-the-lost-with-cwod?p=217064#post217064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think you can do different take than the two lines if you treat Changelings as classic Changelings and make them doppelgangers replacing human children spirited away for some reason by some inscrutable beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s already support for this in <b>Dreaming</b>: the Nobles who have returned largely fit this model. Granted, it could be played up more than it is; but OTOH, I wouldn\u2019t want it to become the <i>only</i> choice available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T15:23:34-07:00","id":220488,"title":"","content":"Of all the game lines you can remove from cWoD, C:tD is the easiest to take out. The Mists apparently work on other supernatural as easily as it does mortals. The mage book actually recommended that you write the things that happened to you down while you are still enchanted, because you will forget once the Glamour you were enchanted with runs out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T02:05:38-07:00","id":222985,"title":"","content":"From the classic world of darkness, I think the Midnight Cirkus would work out very well for a Changeling the Lost-game. I haven\u00b4t read much Dreaming, but from what I\u00b4ve seen I definetely prefer Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1298-the-chronicler","name":"The Chronicler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}